IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.06 (compassionate care benefits), 152.061
-- (critically ill child) and 152.062 (critically ill adult). The three sections say the same things about the
-- certificate, the period, the exception, the waiting period and the division of weeks, with different figures; where
-- they do, one rule serves all three and cites all three subsections, as the keel did for s 6(2) and s 152.01(5).
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- What the Regulations decide is a plain input: who is a family member, a critically ill child or adult (reg 1(3), (6),
-- (7), piece er1); the classes of medical practitioner who may issue the certificate (reg 41.2, piece er3); how the
-- weeks are divided when the claimants cannot agree (reg 41.6, piece er3). No regulation was found that prescribes a
-- shorter period for s 152.06(4) or "the prescribed requirements" of the deferral rules.
-- The provincial-law reduction (ss 152.06(9), 152.061(11), 152.062(9)) is the shared rule in ei5-sickness-pregnancy.
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in these sections.

§ `152.06 Compassionate care benefits`

§§ `The certificate (152.06(1), (2) and (4); 152.061(1), (2); 152.062(1), (2))`

-- The certificate may be issued by a medical doctor or a nurse practitioner, or, in the circumstances set out in the
-- regulations, by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners (reg 41.2: a practitioner authorized abroad).
-- src:2245 | (2) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate required under subsection (1) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
-- src:2282 | (2) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate referred to in subsection (1) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
-- src:2319 | (2) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate referred to in subsection (1) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(2), s 152.061(2), s 152.062(2) (src:2245) (src:2282) (src:2319)
GIVEN `is a medical doctor or a nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 41.2 (piece er3)
      `the circumstances set out in the regulations exist` IS A BOOLEAN           -- out of range: reg 41.2 (piece er3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.06(2), 152.061(2) and 152.062(2) the certificate may be issued by the practitioner` IF
        `is a medical doctor or a nurse practitioner`
    OR  (`is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` AND `the circumstances set out in the regulations exist`)

-- Subsection (4): "If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of this section": (a) the certificate must state a
-- significant risk of death within that period instead of the 26 weeks of (1)(a), and (b) that period applies for
-- (3)(b)(iii) instead of the 52 weeks. No regulation prescribing one was found, so NOTHING is the usual input.
-- src:2258 | (4) If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of this section,
-- src:2259 | (a) the certificate referred to in subsection (1) must state that the family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within that period; and
-- src:2260 | (b) that period applies for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(iii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(4) (src:2258-2260)
GIVEN `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.06(4); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.06(4)(a) the number of weeks within which the certificate must state a significant risk of death` IS
    CONSIDER `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 26
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- src:2258 | (4) If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of this section,
-- src:2259 | (a) the certificate referred to in subsection (1) must state that the family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within that period; and
-- src:2260 | (b) that period applies for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(iii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(4) (src:2258-2260)
GIVEN `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.06(4); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.06(4)(b) the number of weeks that ends the period under subparagraph (3)(b)(iii)` IS
    CONSIDER `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 52
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- Subsection (1): benefits are payable to a self-employed person if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued
-- a certificate that (a) a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within 26
-- weeks (from the day the certificate is issued or, if the claim is made earlier, from the day from which the
-- practitioner certifies the condition) and (b) the family member requires the care or support of one or more other
-- family members. The caller measures the weeks of risk from the right day.
-- src:2239 | 152.06 (1) Subject to this Part, benefits are payable to a self-employed person if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate stating that
-- src:2240 | (a) a family member of the self-employed person has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within 26 weeks
-- src:2241 | (i) from the day on which the certificate is issued, or
-- src:2242 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, from the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member’s medical condition; and
-- src:2243 | (b) the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(1) (src:2239-2243)
GIVEN `the person who has the condition is a family member of the self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 1(3) (piece er1)
      `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks within which the certificate states the risk of death` IS A NUMBER
      `the certificate states that the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.06(1) benefits are payable for the care or support of a gravely ill family member` IF
        `the person who has the condition is a family member of the self-employed person`
    AND `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it`
    AND `the certificate states a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death`
    AND `the number of weeks within which the certificate states the risk of death`
            AT MOST `s 152.06(4)(a) the number of weeks within which the certificate must state a significant risk of death` `the shorter period prescribed, in weeks, if one is prescribed`
    AND `the certificate states that the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members`

-- Subsection (3.1): no additional certificate is needed for benefits payable after the 26 weeks, subject to s 50(8.1).
-- src:2256 | (3.1) For greater certainty, but subject to subsections (3) and 50(8.1), for benefits under this section to be payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks set out in paragraph (1)(a), it is not necessary for a medical doctor or nurse practitioner to issue an additional certificate under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(3.1) (src:2256)
GIVEN `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 50(8.1) (piece ei2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.06(3.1) an additional certificate is required for benefits payable after the end of the 26 weeks` IF
    `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate`

-- src:2278 | 152.061 (1) Subject to this Part, benefits are payable to a self-employed person who is a family member of a critically ill child, in order to care for or support that child, if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate that
-- src:2279 | (a) states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members; and
-- src:2280 | (b) sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.061(1) (src:2278-2280)
GIVEN `the person is a family member of a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 1(3), (6) (piece er1)
      `is providing care or support to that child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.061(1) benefits are payable for the care or support of a critically ill child` IF
        `the person is a family member of a critically ill child`
    AND `is providing care or support to that child`
    AND `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it`
    AND `the certificate states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members`
    AND `the certificate sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support`

-- src:2315 | 152.062 (1) Subject to this Part, benefits are payable to a self-employed person who is a family member of a critically ill adult, in order to care for or support that adult, if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate that
-- src:2316 | (a) states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members; and
-- src:2317 | (b) sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.062(1) (src:2315-2317)
GIVEN `the person is a family member of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 1(3), (7) (piece er1)
      `is providing care or support to that adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.062(1) benefits are payable for the care or support of a critically ill adult` IF
        `the person is a family member of a critically ill adult`
    AND `is providing care or support to that adult`
    AND `a certificate has been issued by a practitioner who may issue it`
    AND `the certificate states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members`
    AND `the certificate sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support`

§§ `The period for which benefits are payable (152.06(3) and (5); 152.061(3) and (5); 152.062(3) and (4))`

-- The exception: subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) (the claim made before the certificate is issued) does not apply to a claim
-- if (a) when the certificate is filed all benefits that might have been payable on the claim have been exhausted,
-- (b) the beginning of the period has already been determined and filing would move it to an earlier date, or (c) the
-- claim is made in other circumstances set out in the regulations (none found).
-- src:2262 | (5) Subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:2263 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2264 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined with respect to the family member, and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2265 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
-- src:2294 | (5) Subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:2295 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2296 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2297 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
-- src:2330 | (4) Subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:2331 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2332 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2333 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(5), s 152.061(5), s 152.062(4) (src:2262-2265) (src:2294-2297) (src:2330-2333)
GIVEN `when the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to the claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period has already been determined and filing the certificate would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 152.06(5)(c), 152.061(5)(c), 152.062(4)(c); none found
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.06(5), 152.061(5) and 152.062(4) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` IF
       `when the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to the claim have already been exhausted`
    OR `the beginning of the period has already been determined and filing the certificate would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date`
    OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- The period begins on the first day (Sunday) of the week in which falls (i) the day the first qualifying certificate is
-- issued and filed with the Commission or (ii) where the claim was made before the certificate is issued, the day from
-- which the practitioner certifies the condition (unless the exception applies). It ends on the last day (Saturday) of
-- the week in which the first of these occurs: all benefits payable in respect of the person are exhausted, the person
-- dies, or the period of 52 weeks following the first day of the first week ends (the shorter prescribed period in
-- place of the 52 under s 152.06(4)(b); a caller passes the number of weeks). The 52 weeks following the first
-- Sunday end on the Saturday 52*7 - 1 days later (fork F10).
-- src:2247 | (3) Subject to section 152.14, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:2248 | (a) that begins on the first day of the week in which one of the following falls, namely,
-- src:2249 | (i) the day of issuance of the first certificate in respect of the family member that meets the requirements of subsection (1) and is filed with the Commission, or
-- src:2250 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member’s medical condition; and
-- src:2251 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs, namely,
-- src:2252 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the family member are exhausted,
-- src:2253 | (ii) the family member dies, or
-- src:2254 | (iii) the period of 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a) ends.
-- src:2284 | (3) Subject to section 152.14, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:2285 | (a) that begins on the first day of the week in which either of the following falls:
-- src:2286 | (i) the day on which the first certificate is issued in respect of the child that meets the requirements of subsection (1) and is filed with the Commission, or
-- src:2287 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill; and
-- src:2288 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs:
-- src:2289 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the child are exhausted,
-- src:2290 | (ii) the child dies, or
-- src:2291 | (iii) the expiry of 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a).
-- src:2321 | (3) Subject to section 152.14, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:2322 | (a) that begins on the first day of the week in which either of the following falls:
-- src:2323 | (i) the day on which the first certificate is issued in respect of the adult that meets the requirements of subsection (1) and is filed with the Commission, or
-- src:2324 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill; and
-- src:2325 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs:
-- src:2326 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the adult are exhausted,
-- src:2327 | (ii) the adult dies, or
-- src:2328 | (iii) the expiry of the 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(3), s 152.061(3), s 152.062(3) (src:2247-2254) (src:2284-2291) (src:2321-2328)
GIVEN `the day of issuance of the first certificate that meets the requirements and is filed with the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition` IS A DATE
      `subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which all benefits payable in respect of the person are exhausted` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the number of weeks following the first day of the week at the end of which the period ends` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `ss 152.06(3), 152.061(3) and 152.062(3) the period for which benefits are payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a)`, `the last day of the week in which the period ends`
    WHERE
        `the day that fixes the first week` MEANS
            IF `the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued` AND (NOT (`subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim`))
            THEN `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition`
            ELSE `the day of issuance of the first certificate that meets the requirements and is filed with the Commission`
        `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day that fixes the first week`
        `the last day of the 52 weeks, or of the shorter prescribed period` MEANS
            `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a)` PLUS ((`weeks as days` `the number of weeks following the first day of the week at the end of which the period ends`) MINUS 1)
        `the last day of the week of exhaustion, if it occurs` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which all benefits payable in respect of the person are exhausted`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the 52 weeks, or of the shorter prescribed period`
            WHEN JUST d THEN `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` d
        `the last day of the week of death, if it occurs` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the person dies`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the 52 weeks, or of the shorter prescribed period`
            WHEN JUST d THEN `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` d
        `the last day of the week in which the period ends` MEANS
            `the earlier of` (`the earlier of` `the last day of the week of exhaustion, if it occurs` `the last day of the week of death, if it occurs`)
                             `the last day of the 52 weeks, or of the shorter prescribed period`

§§ `Waiting period and division of weeks`

-- Deferral of the waiting period: until another claim in the same benefit period if (a) another claimant has claimed in
-- respect of the same person during the period and has served or is serving their waiting period, (b) another
-- claimant is claiming at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period, or (c) the self-employed person or the
-- other claimant meets the prescribed requirements (none found in the Regulations).
-- src:2268 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.1 in respect of the same family member during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:2269 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.1 in respect of the same family member at the same time as the self-employed person and that other claimant elects to serve the waiting period; or
-- src:2270 | (c) the self-employed person, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.1 in respect of the same family member, meets the prescribed requirements.
-- src:2300 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:2301 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period; or
-- src:2302 | (c) the self-employed person, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child, meets the prescribed requirements.
-- src:2336 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:2337 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period; or
-- src:2338 | (c) the self-employed person, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult, meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(6), s 152.061(6), s 152.062(5) (src:2268-2270) (src:2300-2302) (src:2336-2338)
GIVEN `another claimant has made a claim in respect of the same person during the period and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant is making a claim in respect of the same person at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed person or another claimant who has made such a claim meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 152.06(6)(c), 152.061(6)(c), 152.062(5)(c); none found
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.06(6), 152.061(6) and 152.062(5) the waiting period may be deferred` IF
       `another claimant has made a claim in respect of the same person during the period and has served or is serving their waiting period`
    OR `another claimant is making a claim in respect of the same person at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period`
    OR `the self-employed person or another claimant who has made such a claim meets the prescribed requirements`

-- The most that may be divided between two claimants: 26 weeks (compassionate care), 35 (critically ill child), 15
-- (critically ill adult).
-- src:2272 | (7) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.1 in respect of the same family member, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.1 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 26 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2274 | (8) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same family member, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.1, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.1 that may be divided between them may not exceed 26 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(7) and (8) (src:2272) (src:2274)
`s 152.06(7) and (8) the maximum number of weeks that may be divided` MEANS 26

-- src:2305 | (8) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.2 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 35 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2307 | (9) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.2, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.2 that may be divided between them must not exceed 35 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.061(8) and (9) (src:2305) (src:2307)
`s 152.061(8) and (9) the maximum number of weeks that may be divided` MEANS 35

-- src:2340 | (6) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.3 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2342 | (7) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same adult, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.3 that may be divided between them must not exceed 15 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.062(6) and (7) (src:2340) (src:2342)
`s 152.062(6) and (7) the maximum number of weeks that may be divided` MEANS 15

