-- src:2274 | (8) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same family member, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.1, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.1 that may be divided between them may not exceed 26 weeks.
-- src:2305 | (8) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.2 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 35 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2307 | (9) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.2, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.2 that may be divided between them must not exceed 35 weeks.
-- src:2340 | (6) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.3 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2342 | (7) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same adult, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23.3 that may be divided between them must not exceed 15 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(7) and (8), s 152.061(8) and (9), s 152.062(6) and (7) (src:2272) (src:2274) (src:2305) (src:2307) (src:2340) (src:2342)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks that may be divided` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits to one of the two claimants` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits to the other claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.06(7) and (8), 152.061(8) and (9) and 152.062(6) and (7) a division of the remaining weeks is within the maximum` IF
    `the weeks of benefits to one of the two claimants` PLUS `the weeks of benefits to the other claimant` AT MOST `the maximum number of weeks that may be divided`

-- The claimants divide the weeks in the manner they agree; if they cannot agree, the weeks are divided in accordance with
-- the prescribed rules (reg 41.6, piece er3).
-- src:2272 | (7) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.1 in respect of the same family member, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.1 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 26 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2305 | (8) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.2 in respect of the same child, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.2 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 35 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2340 | (6) If a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 23.3 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23.3 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by the self-employed person and the other person. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.06(7), s 152.061(8), s 152.062(6) (src:2272) (src:2305) (src:2340)
GIVEN `the two claimants agree on a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weeks I am to receive under the division they agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks I am to receive under the prescribed rules` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 41.6 (piece er3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.06(7), 152.061(8) and 152.062(6) the weeks of benefits to be paid to a claimant after the division` IS
    IF `the two claimants agree on a division`
    THEN `the weeks I am to receive under the division they agreed`
    ELSE `the weeks I am to receive under the prescribed rules`

§§ `Benefits that cannot be paid together (152.061(10) and (10.1); 152.062(8))`

-- Benefits under s 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of a child (or an adult) during the period established in
-- respect of that child (adult) under 152.061(3) or 23.2(3) (152.062(3) or 23.3(3)).
-- src:2309 | (10) Benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of a child during the period referred to in subsection (3) or 23.2(3) that is established in respect of that child.
-- src:2344 | (8) Benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of an adult during the period referred to in subsection (3) or 23.3(3) that is established in respect of that adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.061(10), s 152.062(8) (src:2309) (src:2344)
GIVEN `the benefits are under section 23.1 or 152.06` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are in respect of the child or adult for whom the period has been established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period established in respect of that child or adult` IS A `Period of days`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.061(10) and 152.062(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of the child or adult on a day` IF
        `the benefits are under section 23.1 or 152.06`
    AND `the benefits are in respect of the child or adult for whom the period has been established`
    AND `the day` `the day in question` `falls within` `the period established in respect of that child or adult`

-- Benefits under s 23.3 or 152.062 are not payable during the 52 weeks beginning on the first day of the week of
-- 152.061(3)(a), in respect of a person who was a critically ill child, if benefits were paid in respect of that
-- person under s 152.061.
-- src:2311 | (10.1) Benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are not payable during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (3)(a) in respect of a person who was a critically ill child if benefits were paid in respect of that person under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.061(10.1) (src:2311)
GIVEN `the benefits are under section 23.3 or 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid in respect of that person, as a critically ill child, under section 152.061` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.061(3)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.061(10.1) benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are not payable on a day` IF
        `the benefits are under section 23.3 or 152.062`
    AND `benefits were paid in respect of that person, as a critically ill child, under section 152.061`
    AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.061(3)(a)`
    AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.061(3)(a)` PLUS ((`weeks as days` 52) MINUS 1)
